{"name":"Hunter’s Hollow","hex":"#989a8d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hunter","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who hunts game for sport or for food; a huntsman or huntswoman.","A dog used in hunting; a hunting dog."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hunter"},{"term":"hollow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small valley between mountains.","A sunken area on a surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["to make a hole in something; to excavate"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hollow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hunting","blocks":[{"text":"Hunting is the human practice of seeking, pursuing, capturing, and/or killing wildlife or feral animals. The most common reasons for humans to hunt are to obtain the animal's body to consume their meat and useful animal products, for recreation/taxidermy, although it may also be done for other purposes such as removing predators dangerous to humans or domestic animals, to eliminate pests and nuisance animals that damage crops/livestock/poultry or spread diseases, for trade/tourism, or for ecological conservation against overpopulation and invasive species."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Paul_Childerley_driven_hunt_Finland_04.png/330px-Paul_Childerley_driven_hunt_Finland_04.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunting","wikidata":"Q36963"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg/500px-Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg/1280px-Bogenj%C3%A4ger_auf_der_Lockjagd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2